diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index f8b6858..9fc531b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,13 +8,36 @@ All notable changes to the A House Divided desktop client are documented here.
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **SSE kept reconnecting after an intentional disconnect** — `disconnect()` aborts the in-flight request, but the aborted stream's `end`/`error` callbacks fire afterwards and scheduled a reconnect the caller had just cancelled (e.g. right after switching game servers, so the client could reconnect before navigation completed). Reconnect scheduling is now suppressed while intentionally disconnected and resumes on the next explicit `connect()` (`src/sse.js`).
+- **Crash on startup navigation after window close** — the first-load handler awaited the display-mode cookie write, then dereferenced `mainWindow`; closing the window during that await crashed the main process. The window reference is captured up front and re-checked after the await (`src/main.js`).
+- **Deep links / CLI URLs ignored in packaged builds** — argument scanning used `argv.slice(2)`, which is only correct for dev runs (`electron . <arg>`); packaged builds start user args at index 1, so `ahd://` and game URLs passed to a fresh or second instance were silently dropped (`src/main.js`).
+- **PiP / dashboard pollers could hang forever** — the 15-second request timeout was cancelled as soon as response _headers_ arrived; a stalled body left the promise unsettled (stale PiP panels, silent dashboard updates). The deadline now stays armed until the request settles (`src/pip-view-poller.js`, `src/dashboard.js`).
+- **Corrupted non-ASCII API responses** — authenticated JSON bodies were decoded chunk-by-chunk, so multi-byte UTF-8 characters split across chunk boundaries turned into replacement characters (broken names/text). Bodies are now accumulated as raw buffers and decoded once (`src/site-api.js`, `src/error-handler.js`).
+- **Cookie-store failures crashed background polls** — a rejected cookie lookup propagated out of `fetchClientNav`/`postJsonAuthed` as an unhandled rejection in the 30–60s polling timers. Cookie reads that fail now degrade to "no cookies" instead of rejecting (`src/site-api.js`).
+- **Silent shortcut registration failures** — `globalShortcut.register()` reports failure via its return value, not by throwing; combos claimed by another app now log a warning instead of failing silently (`src/shortcuts.js`).
+- **Crash when saving a screenshot after window close** — `saveScreenshotDialog` attached a native save dialog to a possibly destroyed window after the async capture. Guarded (`src/feedback.js`).
+- **Crash when clicking Game menu items with no window** — Reload / Go Home / Clear Cache & Reload / Navigate entries touched `webContents` of a closed or destroyed main window (possible on macOS where the app keeps running without windows). All menu actions now no-op safely; **Clear Cache & Reload** also catches `clearCache()` failures instead of crashing.
+- **Crash when clicking tray items or notifications with no window** — Tray click / Navigate-to entries and notification click / action-button handlers called `show()`/`focus()`/`loadURL()` on a destroyed window. Guarded.
+- **Unhandled promise rejections crashed the main process** — Several floating promises rejected straight into Node's unhandled-rejection handler (fatal dialog): the startup display-mode cookie set, Focused Mode toggle cookie set, command-palette injection, View→Theme page script injection, feedback-dialog script injection, auto-updater check/download promises, and update dialogs shown against a destroyed window. All now have explicit error handling.
+- **Update dialogs after window close** — `promptUpdate`/`promptInstall` no longer attempt to attach a message box to a destroyed window.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Dependencies refreshed to latest** — Electron 44 (current), eslint 10.9.1, globals 17.11.0, jest 30.4.2, prettier 3.9.6, @playwright/test 1.62.1. Removed unused dev dependency `electron-playwright-helpers`. `npm audit` is clean (0 vulnerabilities); transitive bumps applied for brace-expansion, fast-uri, flatted, js-yaml advisories. `electron-store` remains on v8 (v9+ is ESM-only; the main process is CommonJS).
+- **Upstream v1.2.1 fixes folded in** — SSE 404 crash fix from master (safe error emission + endpoint-gone handling) is included in this branch.
 - **Crash on reload with invalid TLS certificate (`net::ERR_CERT_DATE_INVALID`)** — Every main-process navigation went through un-awaited `webContents.loadURL()` promises; when the game server's certificate failed validation (e.g. the sandbox host serving an expired certificate, or a wrong system clock), the rejected promise surfaced as a fatal "A JavaScript error occurred in the main process" dialog. All `loadURL` call sites (Game menu Reload/Go Home, context-menu Reload, IPC navigate/go-home/sign-out, notifications, tray, shortcuts, PiP, pop-out windows, deep links) now go through a new `safeLoadURL` helper (`src/safe-load-url.js`) that logs failures instead of crashing; the existing in-app error overlay still appears via `did-fail-load`.
 - **Certificate-specific error overlay** — `did-fail-load` now distinguishes TLS failures (`ERR_CERT_*`) from other network errors and shows a dedicated message advising users to check their computer's date/time settings or the server's certificate, plus the Chromium error code and a **Retry** button in the overlay.
 
 ### Changed
 
 - **Electron 33 → 44** — Runtime updated from the EOL Electron 33 line to Electron 44 (current Chromium, current security patches). No API changes were required.
-- **electron-builder 25 → 26**, **electron-updater 6.8.3 → 6.8.9**. `electron-store` remains on v8 (v9+ is ESM-only; the main process is CommonJS).
+- **electron-builder 25 → 26**, **electron-updater 6.8.3 → 6.8.9**.
+
+## [1.2.1] - 2026-08-25
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **SSE 404 no longer crashes the app** — The web app removed the `/api/events` SSE endpoint (replaced by polling), so the client's SSE connection received a permanent 404 on every page navigation. `src/sse.js` emitted a Node `'error'` event with no listener attached, which throws as an uncaught exception in the main process and showed the "A JavaScript error occurred in the main process" crash dialog (error spam after Login with Discord redirects). Errors are now emitted through a safe helper that logs instead of throwing, 404/410 responses are treated as endpoint-gone (the existing 30-second fallback polling engages, no pointless reconnect loop), and `src/main.js` forwards SSE errors to the renderer's connection status. Regression tests in `tests/unit/sse.test.js` reproduce the exact reported 404 scenario (ticket #1182).
 
